<%#
  The status badge, in one place: `render({ partial: "shared/status-badge",
  locals: { status } })`. Every page that shows a story or RFC status calls
  this rather than writing `<span class="badge s-...">` itself — which is the
  duplication ringo carries today (`webhook/story.go:656`, and the same markup
  again on the RFC pages).

  `status` is whatever the record holds, which is why the unknown arm exists:
  ringo renders `s-unknown` for a dep whose RFC is missing
  (`webhook/story.go:551,684`), and a null column reaches here the same way.

  The status normalisation below sits in the template because `app/helpers` is
  inert in the vendored trails: a controller's `_helpers` never reached the
  view's scope chain. That was filed from here and is fixed upstream in
  trails#7558; trailmap still pins `7cece02d`, so it lands here with the pin
  bump — `bump-vendored-trails-for-testcase-request-bodies` (RFC 0136), which
  moves this line onto `ApplicationHelper`. The partial stays either way.
%>
<% const shown = String(status ?? "").trim() || "unknown"; %>
<span class="badge s-<%= shown %>"><%= shown %></span>
